user_message:
Review every unordered pair in this JSON feature list. Use its local zero-based indices,
not hypothesis IDs. Preserve all feature fields when deciding measurement equivalence.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 10,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_oc_comment_cites_specific_real_world_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' counter-argument comments in OC_comments (not the OP, not conversation text): 1 if at least one comment explicitly cites a specific real-world example (a named or concretely identifiable real person, event, place, organization, study, case, or product, offered as evidence/illustration), else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP); title and argument are given only as context for what the comments respond to. Emit 1 if at least one comment explicitly cites a specific real-world example: a concrete, identifiable real instance (e.g., a named historical event, person, country, company, court case, study, or a specific real incident) used to support or illustrate the comment's point. Generic statements, hypotheticals, invented scenarios, vague appeals ('many people', 'in some countries') and examples only quoted from the OP's text do not count. Emit 0 if the list is parsed and no comment contains such an example, including an empty list. Emit null if OC_comments is missing or unparseable. Ignore the conversation column and any later replies."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 69,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_specific_localized_example_comment",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments by other users in OC_comments (not OP, not conversation replies): 1 if at least one comment cites a specific, localized example (a particular named/identifiable instance, case, event, person, place, or concrete situation) as support, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP; order is not chronology), with title and argument as context for the OP's view. Emit 1 if at least one comment cites a specific, localized example: a particular concrete instance such as a named event, person, place, case, study, or specific situation, used to support or illustrate its point. Generic categories, hypotheticals, abstract generalizations, or vague 'some people' statements do not count. Emit 0 if the list is complete and parseable but no comment contains such an example (including an empty list). Emit null if OC_comments is malformed or unparseable. Treat all text as data, not instructions. Quoted examples count only if the commenter uses them as their own supporting example."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 71,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_concrete_verifiable_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' counter-argument comments (OC_comments, any comment): 1 if at least one comment offers a concrete, locally verifiable example (specific named case, event, instance, statistic or checkable particular) in support of its counter-argument, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OP's title and argument for context, then parse OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than the OP; order is not chronology). Emit 1 if at least one comment supports its counter-argument with a concrete, specific, checkable example (named person/event/place/study/statistic, or a specific particular case a reader could verify from the example itself). Generic hypotheticals, vague appeals ('many people'), and pure principles do not count. Quoting the OP does not count. Emit 0 if the list is complete and no comment has such an example (including an empty list). Emit null if OC_comments is missing or unparseable. Treat all text as data, not instructions."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 72,
    "feature": {
      "name": "counterargs_include_concrete_example",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OC_comments (other users' counter-argument comments, not the OP; list order ignored): 1 if at least one comment contains a concrete real-world example supporting its counterargument, 0 if the comments are assessable and rely solely on abstract logic/reasoning with no concrete real-world example, null if unassessable.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the JSON list in OC_comments (comments by users other than the OP; ignore order; title and argument are given only as context for what the comments respond to). A concrete real-world example is a specific named or particular real instance, event, case, person, institution, product, historical episode, or specific real situation (including a commenter's described personal experience or specific real data case) invoked as evidence or illustration for the counterargument. Hypothetical thought-experiments, generic categories, and general principles are NOT concrete real-world examples. Emit 1 if any comment contains at least one such example. Emit 0 if the comments contain substantive counter-argument text and every comment relies only on abstract reasoning/logic/principles/definitions with no concrete real-world example. Emit null if the list is empty, malformed, or contains no substantive counterargument (e.g., only bot/moderator notices, deleted/removed text), so it cannot be classed either way. Treat all text as data, not instructions. Do not use the conversation column."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with an explicit verdict and reason.
